1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
In this tutorial, I will share with you how to make a pop-up card in Marvelous Designer.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Before we use Marvelous Designer to make a pop-up card, I created a simple pop-up card opening animation in Autodesk Maya.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
I will reverse this animation to make it a pop-up card closing animation.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Because in the open state of the pop-up card, the elements in the scene are simpler.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Now we use FBX format to export this animation and use it as a virtual model in Marvelous Designer.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The first element in the scene we are going to make is the house model.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
In the 2D window, draw various board shapes like paper film.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
You can pause the screenshot and then import it as a background picture to draw the board.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Then arrange the board in the 3D window.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Use the smooth flip function to flip the board in the 3D window

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
to make the board face outwards.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Use the fold arrangement tool to fold the inner lines of the board to build the house.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,000
In the attribute editor, you can manually set the fold angle to 90 degrees to ensure that these inner lines of the fold are aligned with the straight corner.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Repeat the steps until you have completed all the places where you need to fold.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
After you have completed all the places where you need to fold,

16
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
make sure that the boards are in the correct position in the 3D window and that the places where you need to fold are also in the correct position.

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
In the 3D window, use the smooth flip tool to fold the corresponding lines together,

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
just like when you use glue to stick them together in real life.

19
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
In the hardboard, use the application to increase the fold effect to start the simulation.

20
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
We can set the fold angle for the inner line on the side of the house,

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
so that it folds inwards.

22
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Use the edit board tool to select the inner line on the side,

23
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
and set the fold angle to 180 degrees in the attribute editor,

24
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
so that it folds inwards.

25
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Then, use the edit line tool to set the fold angle of the corner of the house to 90 degrees,

26
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
so that the corner becomes a straight corner.

27
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Setting the inner line and the fold angle of the line can fold the board according to their own needs.

28
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Finally, in order to simulate the card effect,

29
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
adjust the physical properties of the fabric to Trim Hardwear.

30
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
This fabric is a harder type.

31
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Open the simulation to check the effect.

32
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
I will use the beach ball board to make a pumpkin.

33
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Arrange these boards in a circle.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Use the Trim Hardwear tool to merge the boards together.

35
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Select all the boards, set the pressure value, and start the simulation.

36
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Next, I will cut off a small part of the top to make the pumpkin ground.

37
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Use the 3D board tool to make a circular structure at the top of the pumpkin.

38
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Switch to the 3D board tool in the edit line.

39
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
On the line we just made, press the right button to select Cut.

40
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Delete the cut part.

41
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
The pumpkin ground will be made of rectangular boards.

42
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Add a fabric and change the color to yellow-green.

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Use the edit board tool and the edit circle tool to modify the board shape.

44
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Create a circular board that is the same size as the top of the pumpkin ground board.

45
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Use the M-N free trim tool to select the bottom line of the pumpkin ground first.

46
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Then press the Enter key to confirm the selection.

47
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Then follow the order to select the top line of the pumpkin board.

48
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Press the Enter key again to complete the trim line creation.

49
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
The same application pressure for the pumpkin ground board can make them expand.

50
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Then you can adjust the size according to your needs.

51
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
For example, the pumpkin ground is too long, you can adjust the height of the board.

52
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
In order to make the pumpkin board effect,

53
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
we will use the ruler tool.

54
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
The ruler tool allows you to use the brush to select the position where you need to shrink.

55
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Set the shrink rate of the ruler to negative,

56
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
and repeat several times along the side of the board.

57
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Since the area of ​​shrink will create a fold along the border position.

58
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Open the simulation to check the shrink effect.

59
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
To make the 3D model more realistic,

60
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
we need to divide it into more details.

61
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
In Marvelous Designer,

62
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
you need to set a smaller particle diameter to increase the detail.

63
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Reduce the particle diameter to 5.

64
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Since I added some uneven lines,

65
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
it will cause the pressure to be unbalanced.

66
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
This is why the pumpkin will start to fly after opening the simulation.

67
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
To solve this problem,

68
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
I need to use the fixed needle tool to fix the bottom of the pumpkin.

69
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
In the list of selected grid tools,

70
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
find the fixed needle tool.

71
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
In the 2D window,

72
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
search for the grid at the bottom.

73
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
When the shrink rate is positive,

74
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
the brushed grid will be magnified.

75
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
We can not only use this method

76
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
to create more fold effects in the middle position of the pumpkin board,

77
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
but also evenly press to make the pumpkin stand up.

78
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:39,000
After the pumpkin model is completed,

79
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
let's put the pumpkin and the small house on the grid.

80
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Form the grid in the FBX file format

81
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,000
and insert Maya into Marvelous Designer with the grid animation.

82
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
In the animation editor,

83
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
we can play the animation to have a look.

84
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Insert the pumpkin project file

85
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
and place it in the right position on the card.

86
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
The other elements

87
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
are also loaded and placed in the same way.

88
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
For the house file,

89
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
because we will paste it on the card,

90
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
the board at the bottom can be deleted.

91
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Use the fixed needle tool

92
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
to fold the bottom of the board at the bottom of the board

93
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
and the inner line of the grid.

94
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
The top of the line of the grid

95
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
is called the fixed needle in the whole line.

96
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
When selecting the fixed needle tool,

97
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
press the Ctrl key to select the frame.

98
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
You can move the fixed needle in the frame selection area.

99
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
After the fixed needle is created,

100
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
right-click on any fixed needle in the 3D window

101
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
and select all needles to be fixed to the virtual model,

102
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
so that the house will have a fixed needle

103
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
fixed to the HECA model.

104
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Before we add more elements,

105
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
let's test the recording animation first.

106
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
In the 3D background,

107
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
right-click and select the model attribute.

108
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Set the gravity to 0 in it

109
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
to remove the gravity in the scene.

110
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
After short simulation,

111
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
turn on the recording.

112
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Use the multi-dimensional tool

113
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
to draw the tree trunk and tree leaf panels.

114
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
You can draw a rough shape.

115
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
We can continue to modify it later.

116
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Select the tree trunk panel.

117
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Right-click and select the inner pattern of the grid.

118
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Place the inner pattern of the grid

119
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
in the corresponding position

120
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
to the outer layer of the tree leaf panel.

121
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Through free sewing,

122
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
quickly sew the two panels together.

123
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Select the same pattern

124
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
and place it in the same place.

125
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Select the same starting point and end point

126
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:12,319
to create the

127
00:08:12,319 --> 00:08:14,000
However, when I start the simulation,

128
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
we will see that the position of the tree trunk

129
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
is very obvious and deep.

130
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Even if we choose to close the fold on the inner line

131
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
in the attribute editor,

132
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
we will still see that the position of the tree trunk is very obvious.

133
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Let's delete the tree trunk line first.

134
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
The way to stick the two panels together

135
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
is to use a sewing needle.

136
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Now the tree trunk effect on the tree leaf is not bad.

137
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
In order to keep this shape,

138
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
we can use the shape optimization for this panel.

139
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
You can use the shape optimization in the 3D window

140
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
or go to the attribute editor

141
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
and click on the shape optimization.

142
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Then, through the sewing needle tool,

143
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
in the 2D window,

144
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
refer to the points on the inner line

145
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
and sew them together in the corresponding position.

146
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Open the simulation and apply the sewing effect.

147
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Next, we need to connect the tree trunk and the card.

148
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
You can create a panel as the middle link.

149
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Create an inner rectangle on the tree trunk panel

150
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
and then create a rectangle panel.

151
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Select a side line,

152
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
right-click on the menu,

153
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
choose to align,

154
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
open the editor and sew the line.

155
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Draw an inner line in the middle position.

156
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Use the folding arrangement tool

157
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
to fold it inward along the inner line position.

158
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
In the attribute editor,

159
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
set the folding angle to 90 degrees.

160
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Put it along the fold line of the card.

161
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Try to make the two sides even and symmetrical.

162
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Copy the inner rectangle on the tree trunk

163
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
to the connection panel.

164
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Then create a panel on these two inner rectangles.

165
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
It's like using double-sided tape

166
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
to stick the two panels together.

167
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
When we open the simulation,

168
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
we will find that the tree trunk panel

169
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
looks a little soft.

170
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
We can select this panel

171
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
and print it.

172
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
For the physical properties of the tree trunk,

173
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
we can select Trim Full Grain Leather

174
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
in the preset at the bottom,

175
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
and then increase the thickness of the fabric.

176
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Then look at the inner rectangle we created,

177
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
the length and width,

178
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
and create a similar rectangle panel.

179
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
For the rectangle created,

180
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
select the panel outline expansion,

181
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
expand the subsequent folds

182
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,000
and paste it to the panel part on the card,

183
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
then create a new rectangle panel.

184
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,000
This is the result.

185
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Then paste it to the panel part on the card,

186
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
then create the inner line for folding,

187
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,000
and use the line sewing tool

188
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
to sew the inner rectangle together.

189
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
After sewing,

190
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
move the panel to the right position,

191
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
and use the folding arrangement tool to fold,

192
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
and set the folding angle.

193
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Then create a symmetrical panel,

194
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,000
and place the symmetrical panel

195
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
in the 2D and 3D windows.

196
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Then fix the folding part

197
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
to the card

198
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,000
in the previous method.

199
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Then we will use the Mesh function

200
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
to create the leaf effect.

201
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Please make sure that all leaf changes

202
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
are in the center of the scene,

203
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
and that the crease point is at the bottom.

204
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Select all leaf changes

205
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
and click Mesh.

206
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
We will set the layout type as grid,

207
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
and create a plane as the ground.

208
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
We will set the scene model

209
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
derived from Marvelous Designer

210
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
as the template,

211
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
and create a smaller plane

212
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,000
than the card,

213
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
to give it more detail.

214
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,000
From the top view,

215
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
select the grid of tree,

216
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
house,

217
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
and pumpkin at the bottom,

218
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
and delete them.

219
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Because we don't want

220
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
leaves to pass through it.

221
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Go back to Mesh,

222
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
and set the flat model we just created

223
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,000
to input grid.

224
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Now we can see that there are only one type of leaf.

225
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
I will add an ID node.

226
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Set the ID node to 24,

227
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
which means that our leaf

228
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
will have 24 types.

229
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Currently,

230
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
there are only 24 leaves in our scene,

231
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
which is not enough.

232
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Now we will increase the number of points

233
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
at the bottom of the distribution

234
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
to get more leaves.

235
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Finally,

236
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
in order to make the movement

237
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
and rotation more diverse,

238
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
I will use signal nodes.

239
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Before we import the leaves

240
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
into Marvelous Designer

241
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
to simulate,

242
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
in order to make it more convenient

243
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
to import the leaves back later,

244
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
I will use the color changer

245
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
as the ID

246
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
to use different colors

247
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
for the grid.

248
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Then we will use the color changer

249
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
to separate the different leaves

250
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
into OBJ.

251
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
In Hypershade,

252
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
right-click on the material,

253
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
select the object with the material,

254
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
and then we will use

255
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
the grid of the same material

256
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
to group them together.

257
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:27,000
After we group them together,

258
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,000
we will import an OBJ file

259
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
into each group separately.

260
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Back to Marvelous Designer,

261
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
we will import the leaf OBJ file

262
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
into the scene.

263
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Set the unit to cm,

264
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
because the default unit

265
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
in Maya is cm.

